But maybe to make it even more explicit, I can register plugins lazily on first mode use: e.g., in VizWidget, `useEffect(() => { settings.set({plugins: [...]}) })` — but the docs warn: "Rendering <ChartKit> before settings.set({plugins: [...]}) — the global plugin registry must be populated at app entry; an unregistered type throws at render time." So safest: register both plugins at entry (main.tsx), and rely on chartkit's built-in React.lazy for engine bundle laziness. I can additionally guard by ensuring settings.set in a module imported by main.tsx before App render. Since settings.set at module scope in `registerPlugins.ts` imported from main.tsx — fine.

