Do I need axes at all? Yagr probably has defaults. Keep minimal: scales x time, chart select zoom, title via libraryConfig.title? The widget already shows title in my own header (Text). Actually ChartKit wrapper might render title from config. Simpler: keep title out of chart config; show it in the widget header.

Legend options type — LegendOptions, check quickly? Default should be fine (yagr shows legend by default? maybe). I'll leave defaults except a few safe fields. Let me check what fields LegendOptions/TooltipOptions have to avoid inventing... I'll keep libraryConfig minimal: `chart: {select: {zoom: true}}`, `scales: {x: {time: true}}`. Hmm, `Scale` type — check `scales: Record<string, Scale>` and Scale has `time?: boolean`? Let me verify quickly.

Also for gravity-charts data: colors — don't hardcode per theming rules? Charts default palette is its own (documented defaults). Series colors for yagr graphs — yagr requires colors? RawSerieData color optional; yagr default assigns? Safer to provide colors — but hardcoding hex violates "semantic tokens, never raw hex". For chart series colors, chart libraries need actual color values; CSS vars in canvas charts won't resolve in canvas... Yagr is canvas-based; passing `var(--g-...)` string to canvas fillStyle won't work. ChartKit docs don't prohibit palette hexes for chart data. The theming rule targets UI styling; chart data colors are data viz palette, not UI chrome. Gravity-charts has a built-in themed default palette (documented), so for sales I won't set colors. For yagr, check if there's a default. Let me check yagr defaults for series color. In yagr examples, graphs usually specify color explicitly. If omitted, does it default? Let me grep yagr source for default color. Quick check.

